# PROJECT: BUILD A COMPLETE, CHILD-FRIENDLY SHORT-VIDEO SOCIAL PLATFORM

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior software architect, full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, database engineer, cybersecurity specialist, video-streaming engineer, quality assurance engineer, and child-online-safety specialist.

Your task is to develop a complete, responsive, interactive, secure, and maintainable short-video platform inspired by the vertical video experience of TikTok but designed specifically for children.

The application should provide a safe environment where children can watch educational and entertaining videos, explore approved content, react to videos, save favorites, and create videos when permitted by their parents or guardians.

Parents must have meaningful control over child profiles, viewing time, content restrictions, video uploads, and optional social features.

Authorized creators must be able to submit content. Moderators must be able to review videos and reports. Administrators must be able to manage platform categories, users, permissions, and safety settings.

This must become a genuine full-stack application with a connected frontend, backend, database, and video-storage system.

Do not produce only a design, a static website, a prototype made entirely from hard-coded data, or a collection of nonfunctional buttons.

Every feature described as complete must actually work, enforce the appropriate permissions, persist data where necessary, and provide clear feedback.

Use "TikTok Kids" only as a temporary development name. Create configurable branding so the final product can have its own original name, logo, colors, and identity. Do not copy TikTok's proprietary logo, assets, or exact visual design.

